keel-mariadb (0.1.1) trixie; urgency=high

  * Keep the socket units of mariadb-server off (keel-mariadb#29). Debian's
    mariadb.socket has ListenStream=3306, which systemd binds as [::]:3306.
    The first boot of systemd enables every unit that no preset disables,
    and pct create of Proxmox VE makes the first start of a container a
    first boot. On such nodes the socket held 3306 on every address, the
    server got its listeners from systemd, bind-address had no effect, and
    3306 answered on the public uplink. The manifest says expose: mesh.
  * Ship /usr/lib/systemd/system-preset/20-keel-mariadb.preset, which
    disables mariadb.socket and mariadb-extra.socket at a first boot.
  * postinst masks both units with deb-systemd-helper on configure, for a
    machine whose first boot already ran. It does not stop an active socket
    or restart the server; that occurs at the next start of the machine, or
    when the operator restarts the server. postrm removes the masks it made,
    on purge only.

 -- Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 01:00:00 +0000

keel-mariadb (0.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * First release (handbook decision 0041; keel-mariadb#25). Ships the
    appliance manifest of Keel MariaDB as
    /usr/share/keel/appliances/mariadb.yaml: base core, whose five overlays
    (installer, wireguard, etcd, crowdsec, vip) it inherits with their
    states and adds none; the MariaDB server as its own process,
    mariadb.service on 3306 as a mesh port, with a Monit mysql check that
    restarts it; the db_password secret (generate allowed, shared, since
    the mysql database replicates with the rest) that firstboot.d/35mysqlpass
    sets the administrative account from; and the db_user option, default
    admin, with the account name rule of lib/mariadb.sh. Without it the
    image had only core.yaml, so appliance.name: mariadb was refused and
    keel inspect inferred core.
  * Depends on keel-core (>= 0.1.3), the first that carries the vip overlay
    a pair needs, keel (>= 0.23.0), the first that configures the pair of
    docs/replication.md, and mariadb-server, whose unit the manifest names.

 -- Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0000
